			<div class="content" id="post-content-4579365">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> History, Possibly Certain Horror Aspects</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Special Containment Procedures, Description, Addenda describing the Life and Times of a user of the Book, Experiment Log, Exploration Log.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> It’s a book that whenever you write a hypothetical scenario in it, it will come true. For example, writing “What if Germany won WW2?” Will transport you to a world where Germany has won WW2. The book will transport itself AND the user to this world, so to return, you could say; “What if I returned to my original world?”</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Narrative&nbsp;and&nbsp;Hook</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The first part will revolve around a journal of a man, named Cody, who wrote a hypothetical scenario in the book, “What if Germany won WW1?” He is transported to a parallel world in 2020, in which the world has changed dramatically from what we’ve come to know. Cody would document his experiences in the journal, talking about historical events that would’ve otherwise never happened in our timeline. He talks of the 1920 British Revolution, the failed 1970 Russian Revolution, the Second American Civil War, and other events that the article will go further into detail about. After looking through the journal, the Foundation will commence an interview with Cody asking the nature of the book. When questioned on how we returned to the real world, he claims he wrote, “What if everything went back to normal?”</p>
<p>After this, I plan to introduce a test log involving a scientist and security guard in physical contact while the scientist writes a hypothetical scenario. After entering that world, it is shown that the MTF Unit and the scientist’s contact have worked to allow access to this world for both of them. As such, the Foundation will begin sending Class-D personnel with escort from MTF Units into worlds which they wish to research. These journeys will be documented and presented in the form of notes by the Class-D.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Alternate history is a topic which has been touched on before, but has lots of untapped potentials if done correctly. I believe this article has the potential to draw in readers with big hypothetical questions like the ones described above. The narrative has endless potential and I plan to exploit that potential to make multiple stories about the exploration of these alternate worlds, in addition to the main piece about Cody.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The planned article will be very long, so I feel it would be a bad idea to put all of my plans out there. If you want to here some, feel free to ask for some more!</p>

