														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4580203">
									

<p>Alternate history is really cool, and I think you could tell some great stories with this. However, I'm concerned about content bloat. You seem to have a lot of directions you want to explore. If you get too bogged down in details within the main article, then the suspension of disbelief falls apart and your concept becomes too contrived. I think you'd be best served by sticking to brief overviews of each alternate history in the main piece. Stick to the highlights. If you really want to talk about the intimate workings of each world, you might expand on them through tales later.</p>
<p>With all this in mind, I give you a <span style="color:green;"><strong>greenlight.</strong></span></p>

