			<div class="content" id="post-content-4580720">
									

<p>Alternate History, I've got similar concerns to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rioludoodle" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3165531); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3165531&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1585967850" alt="rioludoodle" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3165531)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rioludoodle" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3165531); return false;">rioludoodle</a></span> but I'd personally take them in a different direction.</p>
<p>Firstly, I think you should focus on the history of one particular theme or country. The history of war, or the history of Empire, or the history of Japan, for some examples. I'd argue that this reduces bloat, and also allows you to do some in-depth exploration of topics.</p>
<p>Secondly, remember to keep in-mind the whacky anonalous alt-history we have going on, including the Mekhanite-Sarkic collapse during the Late Bronze Age, and the Daevite civilisation before that. Endless possibilites with a bit of research.</p>
<p>All in all though, <strong><span style="color: green">Greenlight</span></strong>. Solid concept, and you've got a solid grasp of the subject. Good stuff.</p>

